<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nongda Lairen Pakhangba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">trad. 33 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nongda Lairen Pakhangba is the first king of Manipur in the royal chronicle, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheitharol-kumbaba">Cheitharol Kumbaba</a>, which dates his accession to 33 CE. He is regarded as founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ningthouja-dynasty">Ningthouja dynasty</a> and of the Meitei state centred on Kangla in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imphal">Imphal</a> valley. In Meitei religion he is also identified with the deity Pakhangba, often shown as a serpent-dragon.</p></div>
